l you hit on a conundrum jane there  which is could it so we have actually  got to act on the data that we have and  that's the decision that we've made this  time the most important thing that we've  done is to build up this booster program  to make sure that everybody can get  access to a booster as soon as possible  so if i could just use the time to urge  everybody who hasn't to please come  forward for one of those two million  appointments this week if you haven't  already had one but of course one  there's been many things we haven't  known we didn't know at the beginning  the severity of the data of the of the  disease and now we've we've had some  good news on that of course we don't  know um  about this particular strain and the  impacts uh longer term we do know a bit  about long coverage which is why we've  set up some long coverage clinics and we  are very concerned to make sure that we  uh obviously take care of people who  have long coverage it is debilitating  but you know there's there's so many  unknowns that all we can do is act on  the data that we have because we have to  be balanced and proportionate we know it  is not easy to lock down a country we  know it comes with costs and  consequences to lives to livelihoods to  life chances for children it isn't an  easy decision it's not one to be taken  lightly and that's the balanced and  proportionate approach that we've taken  but it has to we have to act on the data  we have  on the data on boosters as you did bring  them up  why are there are still nine million  people in the uk that haven't had their  boosters and i know that you're  keen to bang on about about all the the  availability of boosters but but only  less than 20 000 people took up that  offer on saturday just gone um yes you  had some days in december with big  numbers but it's fallen off a cliff  since then why have people stopped  getting their booster do you think and  why isn't the government doing more to  get them in  well we are obviously we have a big big  program of  of booster programme all across the  country so it's very convenient it's  very easy to get your booster um well i  think there's probably a little bit of a  bank holiday lag obviously we're all  just back now to work and school but  there is also probably another factor  that i know in my own case there's some  people who are still having to wait out  their 28 days because they actually have  had covered as well so i would expect  those people there was a big surge of  people that had covered during december  and over christmas period so they'll  have to wait 28 days so i suspect that's  probably also having an impact on some  people's ability to get the job straight  away but we would urge everybody if  you're eligible if you are within that  28 days if you've had covered please  come forward and please come forward the  quicker we can get everybody boosted the  better we can really be prepared to what  to ride that wave that the prime  minister talked about it's one of the  key parts of our defense our wall of  defense and we're really relying on this  as a national mission for everybody to  come forward please to get their booster  or if they haven't yet been vaccinated  to come forward and get their jab we  know they work and they make a massive  difference

